{
  "case_id": "2006-06-84",
  "document_hash": "e54cdf88147f9261853762a95e6c11378c8432377e4b94892daff835df24047d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-06-84",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e54cdf88147f9261853762a95e6c11378c8432377e4b94892daff835df24047d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e54cdf88147f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first this morning in 06-84, Safeco Insurance Company versus Burr, and 06-100, GEICO General Insurance Company versus Edo."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2006-06-84",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e54cdf88147f9261853762a95e6c11378c8432377e4b94892daff835df24047d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e54cdf88147f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MAHONEY: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: I'd like to turn first to the Ninth Circuit's interpretation of the term \"willfully\" and its determination that the case had to be remanded for further proceedings to permit an opportunity to explore Petitioners' communications with their counsel. We ask this Court to find that there is no necessity for any such inquiry for waivers of attorney-client privilege because summary judgment should have been affirmed in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Mahoney",
      "case_id": "2006-06-84",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e54cdf88147f9261853762a95e6c11378c8432377e4b94892daff835df24047d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e54cdf88147f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MAHONEY: I believe that there are two certified class actions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-06-84",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "e54cdf88147f9261853762a95e6c11378c8432377e4b94892daff835df24047d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e54cdf88147f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I also ask, do you agree with the Petitioner on the meaning of adverse action?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Millett",
      "case_id": "2006-06-84",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "e54cdf88147f9261853762a95e6c11378c8432377e4b94892daff835df24047d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e54cdf88147f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MILLETT: No, we agree with Respondents on the meaning of adverse action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-84",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "e54cdf88147f9261853762a95e6c11378c8432377e4b94892daff835df24047d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e54cdf88147f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF SCOTT A. SHORR ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENTS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-84",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e54cdf88147f9261853762a95e6c11378c8432377e4b94892daff835df24047d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e54cdf88147f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They're making this argument, and I think you got close to it a minute ago when you alluded to statutory purpose. I think this is what's behind, and you tell me if I'm wrong. One purpose of the statute is to alert a consumer that the consumer's credit report may contain errors which are doing the consumer some kind of damage."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Shorr",
      "case_id": "2006-06-84",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e54cdf88147f9261853762a95e6c11378c8432377e4b94892daff835df24047d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e54cdf88147f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think it has to be an increase based on some aspect, but the only way to give effect to that statutory purpose is an increase above what you would otherwise qualify for had you had better credit and of course --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-06-84",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e54cdf88147f9261853762a95e6c11378c8432377e4b94892daff835df24047d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e54cdf88147f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "By that you're talking linguistically, but I am interested in the purpose. So I looked up on the Internet approximately what percent of the people have the best credit score and that's about 1 percent. So 99 percent of the public doesn't have the best possible credit score. Now I take it that means that you could in fact, if it's even roughly right, have 99 percent or a little less or even perhaps a little more when they look at that report that, since it's not perfect in 99 percent of the cases, it's quite possible that they won't get the best conceivable rate which might be reserved for just perfect people. And if that's so, in 99 percent of the cases they'll send out notices. And that's why I asked my question about the boy who calls wolf. What will happen if 99 percent of the people who apply for insurance or any other thing get notices? I suspect that this is only intuitive,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-06-84",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e54cdf88147f9261853762a95e6c11378c8432377e4b94892daff835df24047d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e54cdf88147f-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't understand what pertinence that has to my question which is, why do you get to pick the best credit report as the baseline from which you would measure your hypothetical increase?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Mahoney",
      "case_id": "2006-06-84",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e54cdf88147f9261853762a95e6c11378c8432377e4b94892daff835df24047d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e54cdf88147f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If I could start by just responding to the issue of the new document, I just want to emphasize that this document was created by people who weren't lawyers. It was done before GEICO even started using credit to price insurance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-84",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e54cdf88147f9261853762a95e6c11378c8432377e4b94892daff835df24047d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e54cdf88147f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 10:59 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matters was submitted.)"
    },
